{"content":[{"c":["HORSE GATE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Gate near the palace in Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.31.40","r":"Jer.31.40","rawR":"Jer.31.40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.31.40","value":"Jer.31.40"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 31:40"},"), in the southeast part of the city wall. Here Queen Athaliah was put to death (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.11.16","r":"2Kgs.11.16","rawR":"2Kgs.11.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.11.16","value":"2Kgs.11.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 11:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.23.15","r":"2Chr.23.15","rawR":"2Chr.23.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.23.15","value":"2Chr.23.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 23:15"},"). The gate was restored under Nehemiah (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.3.28","r":"Neh.3.28","rawR":"Neh.3.28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.3.28","value":"Neh.3.28"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 3:28"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jerusalem_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jerusalem"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"HorseGate","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jer 31:40","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.31.40","rawQueryValue":"Jer.31.40","sourceRefExact":"Jer.31.40"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 11:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.11.16","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.11.16","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.11.16"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 23:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.23.15","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.23.15","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.23.15"},{"anchorText":"Neh 3:28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.3.28","rawQuery